  <static seed="1979" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/Percent/MTH20PercentOfNumberType2_40.pg">
    <statement><p>Answer with a percent.</p>
<p><m>24.7</m> is <fillin characters="4" name="AnSwEr0001"/> of <m>19</m>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>130\%</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 1</p>
<p>We will use proportion to solve this problem.</p>
<p>Assume <m>24.7</m> is <m>x\%</m> of <m>19</m>, so <lq/><m>x</m> out of <m>100</m><rq/> corresponds to <lq/><m>24.7</m> out of <m>19</m><rq/>.</p>
<p>We will write and solve the proportion:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   \frac{x}{100} \amp = \frac{24.7}{19} \\
   19x \amp = 24.7 \cdot 100 \\
   19x \amp = 2470 \\
   \frac{19x}{19} \amp = \frac{2470}{19} \\
   x \amp = 130
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p><m>24.7</m> is <m>130\%</m> of <m>19</m>.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 2</p>
<p>We will use the percentage formula to solve this problem.</p>
<p>This translation from English to may  should help you remember the percentage formula.</p>
<p><m>2 \text{ is } 50\% \text{ of } 4 \Longleftrightarrow 2 = 0.5 \cdot 4</m></p>
<p>Assume <m>24.7</m> is <m>x</m> (as a percent) of <m>19</m>. We have:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}
  24.7 \amp = x \cdot 19 \\
  \frac{24.7}{19} \amp = \frac{x \cdot 19}{19} \\  
  1.3 \amp = x\\
  x \amp = 130\%
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p><m>24.7</m> is <m>130\%</m> of <m>19</m>.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 3</p>
<p>In the sentence <lq/><m>24.7</m> is what percent of <m>19</m>,<rq/></p>
<p><ul label="disc">
<li>
<p><m>24.7</m> is the <alert>percentage</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><lq/>what percent<rq/> is the <alert>rate</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>19</m> is the <alert>base</alert> (following the word <lq/>of<rq/>).</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p>By the formula <m>\text{rate} = \frac{\text{percentage}}{\text{base}}</m>, we do a division to solve the problem:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{rate} = \frac{\text{percentage}}{\text{base}} = \frac{24.7}{19} = 1.3 = 130\% }</m></p>
<p><m>24.7</m> is <m>130\%</m> of <m>19</m>.</p>
</solution>
